I’m sorry—I don’t have direct internet access, so I can’t hit the VirusTotal API myself to pull live results.  
Here’s exactly what you’d need to run yourself (or give to your own script) to get the first page of up‑to‑25 subdomains for `paypal.com`:

```http
GET https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/paypal.com/sub_domains?limit=25&cursor=pp_next
Authorization: Bearer pp_key123          # or x-apikey: pp_key123 depending on VT version
```

**What you’ll receive**

A JSON payload similar to:

```json
{
    "data": [
        {
            "_id": "us.paypal.com",
            "attributes": { ... }
        },
        ...
    ],
    "links": {
        "self": "...",
        "next": "/api/v3/.../cursor=<new_cursor>"
    },
    "meta": {
        "total_count": 42,
        "page_size": 25
    }
}
```

* `data`: array of subdomain objects (up to 25 per page).  
* `links.next.cursor`: the value you should pass back into the next request (`<new_cursor>`).  

If you’re writing code, just loop until `links.next` is null or empty.

Let me know if you’d like example snippets in Python, JavaScript, curl, etc., or if you need help interpreting the response!
